      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name}  Not working today as usual. \n\nTested links: \n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eu3yoLa3dgs\n\nhttps://www.nicovideo.jp/watch/sm45946615\n\nAnd after I run \"yt-dlp -vU\" in my Windows Powershell, it is giving me this error when I login to the same world and someone is playing video: \n\n2026.04.08 21:51:31 Debug      -  NativeProcess.HasExited: process exited with code 1, took 5519 ms. Command line: C:/Users/User/AppData/LocalLow/VRChat/VRChat\\Tools/yt-dlp.exe (...)\n\n2026.04.08 21:51:31 Warning    -  [Video Playback] ERROR: [generic] Unable to download webpage: HTTP Error 429: Too Many Requests (caused by <HTTPError 429: Too Many Requests>)\n\n2026.04.08 21:51:31 Debug      -  [Video Playback] URL 'https://r.0cm.org/?url=https://youtu.be/OexPEhVAyRs?si=YSYNE0k7OvLj0Yf6' resolved to 'https://r.0cm.org/?url=https://youtu.be/OexPEhVAyRs?si=YSYNE0k7OvLj0Yf6'\n\n2026.04.08 21:51:32 Error      -  [<color=#FF00FF>USharpVideo</color>] Video player error when trying to load https://r.0cm.org/?url=https://youtu.be/OexPEhVAyRs?si=YSYNE0k7OvLj0Yf6\n\n2026.04.08 21:51:32 Debug      -  [Behaviour] Skipping registration of a video player on 'Internals' with the VideoPlayerOverseer as automatic resync is disabled.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
